WEBVTT

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:53.420
Eh? You fought with your father again?

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.890
I went through all that work slicin' up those green peppers fer his omelette

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.550
and he jus' picked 'em all out one by one!

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:03.490
It really makes my blood boil! Next time I'm gonna dropkick him!

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.940
Calm down, you fight because you are on good terms with each other.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.570
Ah, it's Shiori-chan.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:13.230
It is.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:18.990
Shiori-chan, good morning!

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.220
Ah, good morning.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:24.320
So y'can come to school again?

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.290
Yes, I'm feeling much better.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.610
Ah, Shiori-chan's father. Good morning!

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:33.960
Good morning!

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.390
Good morning.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.390
Thank you for visiting Shiori last time.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:41.280
Shiori, you really need to watch yourself.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:41.920
Bye.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.980
What's up? Are ya fightin' with yer father too, Shiori-chan?

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.180
A little.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.560
Oh yeah, yesterday, Onpu-chan came to visit me too.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.780
Oh, that was really nice of her.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.320
But she left after just one minute.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.880
Tearful Memories of Papa and the Fireworks.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:15.080
I'll pass out the kanji test from last week, so come up here when I call your name.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.090
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.750
You all did much better than I expected.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.800
Two people got perfect scores.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.510
Oh? Are those two Fujiwara-san and me again?

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.970
Ah crap...

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.720
I think I got knocked down to Doremi-chan's level.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.950
You were close, Tamaki.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.440
You missed one.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.400
Oh goodness, then who got those two perfects?

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:40.110
Nakayama is amazing, receiving a perfect score after taking so many days off.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.860
Nakayama-san, I see.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:43.780
Shiori-chan, you're awesome!

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:48.320
Harukaze, I think you should worry about your own score for now.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.710
You got the lowest score.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:55.050
No way! I thought I got at least half of them!

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:58.670
You got a 60, but since you forgot to write your name, it's a 0.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.630
You're such a clumsy idiot.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.760
I really am the world's unluckiest pretty girl.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.520
Yer really somethin' else!

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.810
Ya got a higher score than all of us, even after bein' absent fer so long!

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.190
Yeah, I'm so envious.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.650
I think it's because she was sitting next to me.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.640
Ya sayin' she cheated or somethin'?

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.730
I wouldn't do anything like that.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:25.170
You may think you're high and mighty, but you can't just accuse other people like that.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:29.620
Yeah! If she had cheated, she would have gotten a 95 like you did!

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.960
I-I never said anything about cheating.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.460
Oh really? Then what was that all about?

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:40.420
It's so suspicious, getting a perfect score after being out of school for so long.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:44.110
My papa teaches cram school.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:49.100
So he always catches me up when I'm at home.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.040
Now there's no problem.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.980
Tamaki, ya done yet?

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.440
Yes, yes.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.640
Well, havin' a cram school teacher at home sounds great.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:58.870
Well, not really.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:03.340
He's very strict, so he gets angry whenever I get a question wrong.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:04.780
Wow, how barbaric.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.850
Really? My dad lectures me day and night.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:10.930
I'll get lectured when I get into a fight with Pop.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.160
I sometimes get lectured too.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:18.100
I've never been lectured by Papa before, not even once.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.200
Not even once?

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:19.750
Yes.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.460
<i>My</i>  papa is very nice.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.930
So yer sayin' our dads ain't nice?

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.200
Something like that.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.410
What are you gettin' at?

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:32.890
My dad lectures me, but he's also nice to me too!

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.600
Like when he taught me how to play the harmonica.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:36.820
Yeah!

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:42.280
I learned how to ride the bicycle because my dad patiently taught me!

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:46.240
Me too, my papa taught me how to swim.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.200
Those things aren't worth mentioning at all.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:54.660
My papa had private instructors teach me all those things.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.750
Okay now yer really gettin' under my skin!

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:01.000
Tamaki-san, I don't think your father was being considerate in doing that.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:04.430
Love can't be bought with money.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.170
Yeah.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.550
Maybe your papa doesn't really love you.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:12.770
But, it's none of my business.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:22.450
Maybe your papa doesn't really love you.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:33.800
How can my papa not love me?

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:36.080
He gives me anything I want.

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:41.150
Even if I did something wrong, he'd forgive me with a smile.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:45.020
Let's see who can solve these problems.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.170
Tamaki, do the first problem.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:51.390
But Segawa-san said...

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.200
Tamaki!

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:56.890
Tamaki!

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:59.190
Tamaki-san!

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.860
Tamaki, why are you dozing off?

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.070
Go cool your head out in the hall.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.030
Ah... Yes, ma'am...

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.580
Tamaki seems really depressed.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.530
Onpu-chan went a bit too far with what she said.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:21.340
But I'm so envious of Tamaki-san.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:27.150
Because her papa will give her whatever she asks for.

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:28.670
Well, I guess yer right.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.500
My papa is the exact opposite.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:36.090
I wanted to go over to my grandma's house, but he said no.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:39.160
I think that's because your father is worried about your health.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.860
But I'm better already, so he's worrying over nothing.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.600
I told him not to come pick me up...

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:50.570
Don't say that, get going.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:54.780
Well, see you tomorrow.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.740
Goodbye!

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:07.670
Tamaki-san, I don't think your father was being considerate in doing that.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:11.510
Love can't be bought with money.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.590
Maybe your papa doesn't really love you.

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.070
Reika, what's wrong?

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.810
This is your papa's favorite...

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:32.860
What happened?

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.780
I broke your vase.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.870
Reika, are you hurt anywhere?

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.040
I broke it on purpose!

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:43.360
What is the meaning of this, Reika?

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.120
Calm down, it's okay.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.690
Papa, why don't you get mad?

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:49.800
I broke your favorite vase.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.300
Reika...

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.340
I can always buy another vase.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:55.510
I'm fine as long as you're not hurt.

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:04.270
Reika?

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.400
That's not true love!

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.200
You've never loved me!

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:10.680
Reika?

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:11.360
Wait!

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:30.590
Tamaki-san.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.380
Nakayama-san.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.880
What are you doing here?

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.610
N-Nothing.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:42.910
Anyway, is it okay for you to wander about with that weak body of yours?

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:47.780
I fought with Papa, and I'm thinking of running away to my grandma's place.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.540
Wow, you too?

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:50.700
What do you mean?

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:52.830
Ah, it's nothing.

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.360
Anyway, where does your grandma live?

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.490
In Kamakura.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:00.130
Oh? That's near our villa.

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:04.330
Oh yeah, would it be okay if I came with you?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.620
Eh? Really?

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:07.830
But are you sure?

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:13.160
Don't you worry. We're friends, right?

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:14.170
Thank you.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:16.840
Actually I was a bit scared to go all by myself.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.630
Thank you!

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.020
Has Tamaki been here?

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:30.150
Nope.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.980
Did something happen to Tamaki-san?

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:36.190
She had a fight with her father and ran away from home.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:37.400
What!?

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:43.040
I need to go tell the other students, so can all of you go check out the places where she might be?

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:43.960
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:47.830
Meet me at school in an hour, even if you haven't found her.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:48.650
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:54.370
Pop, you heard her, so we'll leave the rest here to you!

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:55.420
Okay!

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:34.120
How did it go, you guys?

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:39.630
Tamaki-san, can you tell us why she left home?

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.130
Actually...

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:47.040
The lights aren't on.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.290
Maybe she's not home?

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:52.320
No way. Grandma! Grandma! Grandma!

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:55.020
What are you girls doing?

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:58.610
I came to visit my grandma, but it seems like she's not home.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:03.340
Ah, she went on a hot springs vacation with her family.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.160
No way...

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:06.840
We can't do anything about that.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:08.870
Let's go to my villa instead.

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:14.210
Because I didn't lecture her, she told me that I don't love her.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.830
That's why she left home.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:18.280
If she broke a vase, ya should be mad at her!

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:20.840
Yeah, you're too nice.

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.260
Really?

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:24.840
I think so too, Tamaki-san.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.360
Maybe that is true.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:32.810
The reason I spoil her like this may be because of what happened seven years ago.

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:37.440
The coffee I make is delicious.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:47.700
R-Reika!

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:58.650
God, please protect my child.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:03.050
The burn wasn't very serious, but I had sworn to myself then,

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:08.660
that I wouldn't make her cry ever again, and that no matter what happened, I wouldn't get mad.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:12.730
And that I would use all my love in her upbringing.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:16.860
But as her father, not getting mad even once is a bit...

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:18.490
That's not true.

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:20.690
I did get mad at her once.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:25.860
It was when there was a fireworks festival near our villa.

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:31.160
I remember that was the summer when Reika was four years old.

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.950
Reika, it's so pretty, isn't it?

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:39.700
Eh? Where's Reika?

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:43.150
Dear!

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:44.050
Reika!

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:49.770
That's dangerous, what if you had fallen!?

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:54.590
Ow!

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:56.660
I hate Papa!

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.610
I-I'm sorry, Reika.

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:08.600
What? Yer just like my dad.

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:10.870
I guess Tamaki forgot all about that.

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:18.040
Ma'am, Shiori left a note that she left home to go to her grandma's house in Kamakura!

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:19.470
What did you say?

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:20.540
Shiori-chan too?

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.080
But Grandma isn't at home!

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:24.300
She's on vacation with her family!

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.960
This is bad.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.460
Seki-sensei!

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:31.930
People saw Tamaki along with someone shorter than her go into the train station!

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:34.060
That must be Shiori-chan!

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.550
Anyway, let's hurry.

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:37.290
Okay.

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:39.450
Everyone, go back home and wait.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:48.560
We bear responsibility for this too.

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:50.340
Let's follow them.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:52.100
We can use magic fer this!

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:05.050
How can we find Shiori-chan's grandma's house?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:09.520
She's not at home, so they're probably not there.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:14.690
Well then, let's use Magical Stage to find out where they are.

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:15.220
Okay!

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:18.570
Pirika Pirilala Carefreely!

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:25.250
Paipai Ponpoi Flexibly!

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:30.450
Pameruku Laruku Proudly!

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:42.900
Magical Stage!

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:52.180
Please tell us where Tamaki and Shiori-chan are!

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:03.690
It's a compass.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:05.400
What does that mean?

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.110
Wait, let me see that.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:12.950
I see, the North Star is over there.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:16.740
This compass points to somewhere else.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:21.000
Maybe it points to where Tamaki and Shiori-chan are?

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.650
I think so too.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:24.740
Let's trust it and find out.

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:25.310
Okay.

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:34.630
I think they're in this villa.

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.200
But it's all dark inside.

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:37.550
Either way, let's check it out.

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:42.030
We rarely come here during winter, so our utilities are cut off.

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:43.330
We can't do anything.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:44.560
There's no food here either.

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:49.650
Wow, it's all because you wanted to go to your grandma's house.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.660
What's wrong, Nakayama-san?

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.660
I-I-It's so cold.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:17:00.030
I feel a little cold too, but you're overdoing it...

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:06.010
What a fever!

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:07.130
Wait right here.

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:11.780
Even Tamaki's got a good side.

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:15.830
But if this goes on, Shiori-chan will be in danger.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:18.110
And we can't use magic to cure her...

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:20.870
But we can use magic to help her with other things.

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:22.520
First, let's get into the house.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:27.690
Pirika Pirilala Poporina Peperuto!

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.250
Turn us into cockroaches!

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:36.950
Noooo, cockroaches again?

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.830
Don't complain, let's go in from the chimney!

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:46.850
The telephone doesn't work! How can I call an ambulance?

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:48.580
What should I do?

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:54.320
Are you okay, Nakayama-san?

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:59.450
We should use magic to make the water and electricity work again.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:17:59.970
Yeah.

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:00.720
Here we go!

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:05.760
Pameruku Laruku Larilori Poppun!

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:09.000
Turn on the lights!

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.440
The electricity is on!

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:18.860
Paipai Ponpoi Puwapuwa Puu!

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.340
Water, come out!

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:25.080
That sound is...

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:27.660
The water is working too!

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:32.280
It's so cold and nice...

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:34.340
Thank you, Tamaki-san.

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:38.790
Okay, my turn!

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:41.780
Pirika Pirilala Poporina Peperuto!

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:44.660
Fireplace, start burning!

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:50.050
W-W-W-Where did this fire come from...!

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:50.800
It's...!

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:54.520
I-I-It's a ghoooooost!

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:57.600
Ya overdid it, Doremi-chan.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:58.540
Sorry.

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:02.370
Tamaki!

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:05.230
So you were here!

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.790
Teacher, there's a ghost!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:11.810
F-Forget about that, Nakayama-san has a fever!

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:13.850
Shiori, are you okay?

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:16.760
I'm fine, Tamaki-san's been taking care of me.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:18.760
You should get to a hospital fast.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:21.490
Tamaki-san, can you take us there?

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:23.850
Sure, I know the way.

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.430
I'm coming along too!

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.320
Now everything's fine.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:37.720
But Tamaki's father hasn't mended things yet.

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:38.860
Let's go too.

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:42.740
It's a slight cold.

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:46.120
She'll be fine after a good night of rest.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.830
Thank you very much.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:52.090
Shiori, do you know how worried I was!?

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:53.290
You are really...

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:55.000
I'm sorry.

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:58.080
Don't scare me like that again.

00:19:58.080 --> 00:19:58.960
Okay...

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:02.350
Everyone, I'm so sorry for all of this.

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:04.610
Please use my car to go back.

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:06.000
Thank you all.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:07.690
I'm not going home!

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:08.430
Reika!

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:15.460
Wait, Reika!

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:18.190
Let go! I don't want to see your face, Papa!

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:20.470
It's time for us to fix things.

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:21.220
Yes.

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:26.700
Pirika Pirilala Poporina Peperuto!

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:30.700
Beautiful fireworks, fire up!

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:34.860
Reika, why don't you understand my feelings?

00:20:34.860 --> 00:20:35.850
I don't understand!

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:37.590
Papa, let go of me!

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:38.210
Reika!

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:58.080
I remember that you hit me like this a long time ago.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:01.110
Yes... during that summer when you were four.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.420
Papa, you actually...

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:04.820
He loves you.

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:09.990
Your father loves you more than anyone else in the world.

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:17.960
Papa!

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:20.550
I'm sorry!

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.360
It's okay, Reika.

00:21:27.590 --> 00:21:30.760
You shouldn't cry.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:31.470
Here.

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:39.030
Let's put up even more!

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:39.850
Okay!

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.500
Kudou Mutsumi is so strong!

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:05.960
No boy in our class can beat her!

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:10.230
Kudou's idol is the pro wrestler, Candy Itou-san.

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:12.510
Oh, breaking news!

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:13.220
Senoo, tell us!

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:17.200
Right! Candy the wrestler said that she'll retire if she loses her next match!

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:18.830
Ehh? Really?

00:22:18.830 --> 00:22:20.660
What will happen to Mutsumi-chan?

00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:23.280
She's been cheering for her so much...

00:22:23.280 --> 00:22:24.480
Ojamajo Doremi!

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:26.270
I Want to Be a Female Pro Wrestler!

00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:29.020
Happy! Lucky! For all of you!
